      "target": {
        "source": {
          "id": "http://cudl.lib.cam.ac.uk/iiif/MS-TS-NS-00298-00055/canvas/1",
          "type": "Canvas",
          "partOf": {
            "id": "https://geniza.princeton.edu/documents/41697/iiif/manifest/"
          }
        },
        "selector": {
          "type": "FragmentSelector",
          "value": "xywh=pixel:3220.15087890625,206.21287536621094,2826.5107421875,3916.670425415039",
          "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/"
        }
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Folio 1r, right side (second section)",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>\n<p>that he was the son of [Yoh\u0323anan? the] Dyer (?). Then [they] placed [in front of him?]</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>the book of magic, and said to him: &ldquo;These books&mdash;are they new or old?&rdquo;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>And he said to them: &ldquo;They are old, and they are the ones that Balaam son of Beor had.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>I found them in the land of Egypt, and anything that is of the utmost attainment (?)&mdash;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>it is with them that it is done. I cure the sick and heal the crippled.&rdquo;&nbsp;They said to him: &ldquo;Why</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>do you use magic and why do you teach people</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>teachings of evil?&rdquo; Then they said to him: &ldquo;Tell us in truth&mdash;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>where did you get these books, or else we will kill you and not show you mercy and will throw</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>your body to the wild beasts.&rdquo; He said to them: &ldquo;My masters, know that these</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>books are not ancient and I did not find them in Egypt, and they are not by Balaam.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>In fact, they are by Yoh\u0323anan the Dyer and he is my teacher.&rdquo; (Pilatus) the governor said</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>to Marinus the elder: &ldquo;Do you know where Yoh\u0323anan the Dyer is?&rdquo; He said</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>to him: &ldquo;He is in Kephar Nah\u0323um.&rdquo; And he (Pilatus) ordered to bring him over. He sent a guard (or, a courtier)</p>\n</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
